Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: a state made with other game files is refused instead of hanging (TODO 304)

A state made with mods (the disc read from Mods\.build\disc, its archives rebuilt) and loaded without them, or the
other way round, loaded: the game's memory holds that disc's layout, its reads went past this disc's end (zeros) and
it waited for them forever - the HQ's "Exit to title screen" stuck in its load. A state now holds the identity of the
game files it has open (size and a hash of the first and last 64 KB, worked out once per file and run; not the memory
cards' files) in a new DISC section, and a load first finds each one as this run reads it (the same tail under this
run's disc folder, then 0177's relocation): another file there and the state is refused before anything is
overwritten - "made with other game files: TFA.ZIP here is not the one it was made with". The files it found are the
ones reopened. A state without the section (made before) loads as before; the format number stays.

